The '''Ika language''' is an [[Igboid language|Igboid]] language, classified under [[Igboid languages|Nuclear Igboid]] in the Yeai [[language family]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Glottolog 4.8 - Ika |url=https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/ikaa1238 |access-date=2023-11-18 |website=glottolog.org}}</ref>

The language is spoken primarily by the Ika people of [[Delta State|Delta]] and [[Edo State|Edo]] states of southern Nigeria.<ref name=":1">{{Cite journal |last=Uguru |first=Joy Oluchi |date=20 July 2015 |title=Ika Igbo |journal=Journal of the International Phonetic Association |language=en |volume=45 |issue=2 |pages=213–219 |doi=10.1017/S0025100315000067 |issn=0025-1003 |doi-access=free }}</ref>

More specifically, the Ika people are in the North-West of Delta State; but some, like Igbanke, Inyelen and Ekpon, are currently in Edo State. Ika communities mostly comprise the following: [[Agbor]], Owa, Umunede, Mbiri, Abavo, Orogodo, Otolokpo, Igbodo, Ute-Okpu, Ute-Ugbeje, Idumuesah, Akumazi, Ekpon, Igbanke, Inyelen, Iru Egbede (Delta State).<ref name=":1" />

Other Ika-speaking communities found in Edo State are Owanikeke, Owa-Riuzo Idu, Igbogili, Ute Oheze, Oghada, Otobaye I & II, Ogan and Ute Obagie N’Oheze. On Delta Radio there is now news in the Ika language. A similar program is also aired on Edo Broadcasting Service (EBS) Radio, where it is called Igbanke Request, named after the most popular Ika-speaking town in Edo State. Ikas have started to write the Bible in their language, and the gospels of Mark, Luke, Matthew and John have been published in Ika along with other books.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2019-04-02 |title=Complete Bible now in Ika language |url=https://www.ikaweekly.com/complete-bible-now-in-ika-language/ |access-date=2023-12-09 |website=Ika Weekly Newspaper |language=en-GB}}</ref> Ifeanyi Okowa is a prominent son of Ika background.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Dr |first=Mefor |date=28 June 2022 |title=Igbo ancestry: Governor Ifeanyi Okowa has nothing to prove |url=https://www.thecable.ng/igbo-ancestry-governor-ifeanyi-okowa-has-nothing-to-prove |newspaper=[[TheCable]]}}</ref>

